Found while working k36 (2026-11-06), against docs.hetzner.cloud/cloud.spec.json: WWW::Hetzner::Cloud::Image has no accessor for image_size, protection, bound_to, created_from, deleted and rapid_deploy; WWW::Hetzner::Cloud::ServerType has none for category. The data arrives in the API response but the entity drops it (no attribute, not in data()). Done = decide per field whether the entity carries it; the ones it carries get an attribute, a data() key, POD and a fixture-backed test.

Decisions (spec: docs.hetzner.cloud/cloud.spec.json, read from a copy outside the repo): all six Image fields and ServerType category are carried, all read-only, no builders. image_size number|null (GB), protection object {delete: bool}, bound_to integer|null (backup images only), created_from {id,name}|null, deleted string|null (RFC3339), rapid_deploy boolean; category string. Values pass through unchanged (JSON booleans stay JSON booleans). Tests use inline mock data plus the images_get fixture (rapid_deploy true); red before (no accessor), green after. Not touched: Server entity still embeds image/server_type as raw hashes.

